==English==
{{wikipedia}}
===Etymology===
{{suffix|cardinal|ity}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cardinalities}}

# {{context|set theory|lang=en}} Of a set, the number of [[element]]s it contains.
#: ''The empty set has a '''cardinality''' of zero.''
# {{context|data modeling|lang=en}} The property of a relationship between a [[database]] [[table]] and another one, specifying whether it is one-to-one, one-to-many, many-to-one, or many-to-many.

